2.2 Main wizard composition

Desktop (1280px and wider)

App shell retains the normal 64px global top navigation. The selected farm/field context is visible but compact.

Main questionnaire container is centred with a maximum width of roughly 1120px and generous 32–40px gutters.

The primary question column occupies approximately 8 of 12 columns. A right-side context rail occupies 4 of 12 columns when the current question benefits from it.

Question card has 28–32px internal padding, 16px radius, default glass fill, 14px blur and subtle border.

Top of the question card: small uppercase section label, question number/stage, large plain-language question, then a one-sentence explanation.

Middle: one main answer control or a small cohesive answer group. Each answer has a clear label and optional short description.

Bottom: “Why we ask” expandable explanation, any evidence suggestion/source status, and navigation controls.

Back remains bottom-left. Continue/Save answer is bottom-right. Save & exit is a consistent secondary action.

The right rail may contain a field context summary, a small map preview, “What we know so far”, data freshness or the explanation of a detected gap. It must never introduce unrelated fields or compete with the main question.

Tablet (768–1279px)

