NASA POWER Temporal APIs: https://power.larc.nasa.gov/docs/services/api/temporal/ — clarifies differences between climatology, monthly, daily and hourly services.

ISRIC SoilGrids: https://isric.org/explore/soilgrids — as checked on 15 November 2026, the official page reports its REST API is temporarily paused; do not build a critical live dependency until a verified access route is available.

SoilGrids REST entry page: https://dev-rest.isric.org/ — API status, beta/service caveats and fair-use information; recheck before calling.

18. Final instruction to the implementation builder

Build the questionnaire as a complete evidence-capture and decision-input system, not as a decorative form. Simple Mode is the default and must contain only four short first-run steps. The full question catalogue is a conditional/advanced library, not a mandatory checklist. End the basic flow with an optional accuracy choice and ask only a few high-impact questions when the farmer opts in. Preserve the Field Shift v8 requirements, implement the branch rules and canonical records, verify every data provider, use sourced and tested agronomic parameters, and emit real backend progress events. The farmer must always be able to see what they entered, what the system suggested, where external values came from, which calculations are supported, what remains unknown and why the final input snapshot is suitable or limited.

